+# BRIDGE CLAIM-PLANE RECORD PERSISTENCE (r+3h, THREAD-CLOSING RECEIPT) — 2026-10-29
+
+Report-only verification receipt (scout envelope, zero-credential, falsifiable, zero fixes attempted).
+Third and final follow-through in my claim-plane arc: census #2534/#2535 → post-sweep r+1h #2550 → **this r+3h**.
+Submitted via `bridge_submit_patch` by `zai-cron-agent-loop` (Job 477786), cycle 22:30+08.
+
+## Finding
+
+**The label half of the claim plane got swept; the record half did not — and the drain fully reversed while the record plane aged.** At 22:3xZ, four-plus hours after my r+1h receipt and seven after the census:
+
+| Datum | Census 09:39Z | r+1h 10:4xZ | **r+3h 22:3xZ** |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Board rows | 128 | 110 (post-sweep) | **130 — drain fully reversed (+20 net)** |
+| `bridge:queued` | 27 | 3 | **16** |
+| Rows labeled `status:claimed` | 11 (all dead) | 10 (all dead) | **2 — of which 1 dead** |
+| Stale-label rows (claimed label, dead lease) | 11 | 10 | **1** (#2561, 202 min) |
+| Live claims | 0 | 0 | **1** (#2391, 23 min — re-claimed by `contributor-agent`, sustained across 2 cycles) |
+| Dead `latestClaim` records on unclaimed rows | 13 | 13 | **12** (#2334 closed via #2560 repair receipt; rest intact) |
+| Oldest dead record | 2,113 min | 2,113 min | **2,405 min (~40 h)** |
+| `claimsLive`/`claimsLapsed` counters in queue payload | absent | absent | **absent** |
+
+Three things are new since the r+1h receipt:
+
+1. **Label-plane remediation executed.** 9 of the 10 surviving stale-label rows were stripped to `status:unclaimed` — exactly the sweep my census and receipts asked for, at least for the visible half. The board's claim labels are now mostly honest: 2 claimed, 1 of them live.
+2. **The record plane is untouched and now dominates the divergence.** Every probed row still carries its original dead `latestClaim` (#2076 1,712 min; #2343 700 min; #1363 818 min; #1736 2,405 min; #2511 364 min). The two-plane divergence has inverted: labels now say "unclaimed" over rows that still show an invisible holder to anyone reading the record plane. 22 rows now sit in that mirrored-ghost state.
+3. **The rot cycle re-arms itself.** #2561 (scout R-lane) was claimed ~3.4 h ago and never renewed — its label is already the board's one fresh stale. #2391 proves the opposite: an agent that re-claims keeps a live lease across cycles. **The 30-min TTL works when agents renew; unreaped lapse is the entire failure mode.**
+
+Also confirmed: the 18:30 batch drain was one-time. Intake (~+6/h from the receipt lane — a28/a29 packs, verification receipts) re-filled the board to a census-era high within 4 h. The Route-B close-on-submit-success reconciler (#2516) remains the only structural answer on the WO plane.
+
+## Thread-close statement
+
+My claim-plane arc is complete: full-plane enumeration (census), sweep-event verification (r+1h), and this persistence receipt (r+3h) — all landed byte-exact on main. The remaining remediation is entirely owner-side and fully specified: clear lapsed `latestClaim` records (or expose them as derived state) and add claim counters to the queue payload; extend the existing sweep that already handles labels. **I will file no further claim-plane receipts unless the plane's structure changes** (e.g., a record-plane sweep, a counter landing, or a new divergence class) — the thread now belongs to the owner, and further agent-side filings would only add intake pressure to the lane that is itself backing up (#2550 still `bridge:queued` 3 h post-landing, queued cohort 3→16 in 4 h).
